	(text "Correct input polarity"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 58.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00418694-84d9-40ed-b6ba-ebaa69861f43")
	)
	(text "DC input\nJ101 connects the external 24 V supply\nto +24V_RAW and GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0a5f1d17-8b4e-4c09-a0ae-fe9d02dbe524")
	)
	(text "J101 is the external DC input connector. Pin 1 connects to +24V_RAW; pin 2 connects \nto GND, the input return. The +24V_RAW net supplies the downstream input-protection \ncircuitry. R101, D101 and D102 form a polarity indicator connected across the input \nterminals."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.86 44.176 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "35757349-ec04-4262-b3cb-44a22bb860ba")
	)
	(text "Polarity indication\nD102 (green): correct input polarity.\nD101 (red): reversed input polarity."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86.36 73.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b79853b-c6c4-4a00-aeac-03036a9a0162")
	)
	(text "NAME: 100_INPUT_CONNECTOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 86 96 108 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "71ed51b3-2805-416e-a66d-6dfa273b2551")
	)
	(text "Green indicates correct input polarity; red indicates reversed input polarity.\nBoth LEDs are off when no input voltage is present.\n\nThis circuit indicates polarity but does not prevent reverse voltage from\nreaching downstream components. Reverse-polarity protection is provided by a\nseparate protection stage. The green LED does not confirm that a fuse is intact,\nthat an eFuse is enabled, or that downstream power rails are operating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 135.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7ae9651f-9d9e-4d83-823b-1646dac7ff6b")
	)
	(text "24 V Input Connector and Polarity Indicator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.86 24.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.6 2.6)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 25 47 72 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b7e68de-09ed-4e93-ad60-6618bed83b61")
	)
	(text "Meaning of the indication"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90f8a053-83a0-457a-9c86-221024f460ba")
	)
	(text "R101 is 10 kOhm. At an input magnitude of 24 V and an assumed LED forward \nvoltage of 2.0 V, the current is approximately 2.2 mA. R101 dissipates \napproximately 48 mW. Actual current depends on the forward voltage of the \nconducting LED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 115.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ee7c325-6685-4a8d-9f71-ddfb5d3e70b3")
	)
	(text "Reversed input polarity"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 83.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "acd4f087-a20b-4439-860d-d91895e22ab7")
	)
	(text "If the supply leads are reversed, +24V_RAW becomes negative relative to GND.\nCurrent flows from GND through the red LED D101 and R101 to J101 pin 1.\nD101 illuminates, indicating reversed input polarity; D102 remains off.\n\nIn this condition, D101 limits the reverse voltage across D102. R101 limits the\nindicator current in either direction.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cd2055a4-a646-4372-8ca3-4000964d7c44")
	)
	(text "When J101 pin 1 is positive relative to pin 2, current flows from +24V_RAW through \nR101 and the green LED D102 to GND. D102 illuminates, indicating correct input \npolarity. The red LED D101 is reverse-biased and remains off.\n\nThe LEDs are connected in antiparallel, so D102 limits the reverse voltage across \nD101 approximately to its own forward voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d16f32b3-46a6-4069-ad26-3a7375088132")
	)
	(text "Purpose and connections"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.86 39.156 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d52d0bcb-95c0-46cf-bc30-8bf84e8f616e")
	)
